# Day 21/50 — DNS (Domain Name System)

Imagine having to remember the phone number of every person you know just to contact them.
Sounds difficult, right?
Of course it is!

The internet has a similar challenge
Computers communicate using IP addresses, but remembering numerical addresses for every website would be inconvenient.

That's where **DNS** comes in

The Domain Name System translates human-friendly domain names, like google.com, into IP addresses that computers can use to locate servers.
We type a name, and DNS helps find its destination.

It's interesting how technology makes complicated things feel simple.

Sometimes, the best systems are the ones doing the difficult work quietly in the background.

**Because simplicity on the surface often takes a lot of work underneath**
